      "extract": "When $t=e^{2\\pi{r}\\sqrt{-1}/N}$ for $r\\in\\mathbb{C}\\setminus{\\mathbb{Z}}$, $J_N\\left(T(a,b);e^{2\\pi{r}\\sqrt{-1}/N}\\right)$ can be given by the following integral form [@Kashaev/Tirkkonen:ZAPNS200 Lemma 1]. $$J_N\\left(T(a,b),e^{2\\pi{r}\\sqrt{-1}/N}\\right) = \\Phi_{a,b,r}(N) \\int_{C} e^{Nf_{a,b,r}(z)} \\tau_{a,b}(z) dz.$$ Here $$\\begin{aligned} \\Phi_{a,b,r}(N) &:=g_{a,b,r}\\sqrt{N}",
